00:05:40.099 --> 00:05:48.560
kind of a very special care very emotional
young young leads but it was just tremendously

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:51.449
well done

00:05:51.449 --> 00:05:57.379
so i called up this fellow whose name was
mitch and i said mitch i read this script

00:05:57.379 --> 00:06:01.919
we'd been co-conspirators we're both starting
out in the business we were friends now new

00:06:01.919 --> 00:06:09.089
friendship and we were excited so he read
it and he called me back he read it on the

00:06:09.089 --> 00:06:14.159
weekend the usual monday morning call back
and he he called me back and said he praised

00:06:14.159 --> 00:06:17.350
it he said this is absolutely gorgeous it
was very emotional it took me back to when

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:23.710
i was that age i had a not dissimilar experience
fabulous thank you it was really really interesting

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:35.539
it's going to be a pass and i said okay mitch
um one favor why why is this a pass you just

00:06:35.539 --> 00:06:40.539
you were just singing at spratuses and it's
because it's too small for stephen i said

00:06:40.539 --> 00:06:48.240
okay that's fair i understand that but let
me ask you a question if you put the script

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:52.589
in steven's briefcase for his weekend read
and he were to come back monday and say to

00:06:52.589 --> 00:06:57.929
you this is a pass would you have any and
specifically whether it's because it's too

00:06:57.929 --> 00:07:04.089
small or otherwise would you have any cause
for embarrassment would it in any way jeopardize

00:07:04.089 --> 00:07:09.809
your standing in the company they said no
it's a brilliant script i said great then

00:07:09.809 --> 00:07:15.699
i am on we're on a phone you can't see me
but i'm on one knee and i am begging you put

00:07:15.699 --> 00:07:26.770
it in steven's briefcase and he did steven
read it and he wanted to buy it now

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:33.400
no one was more stunned than i was but i think
this is a business that turns on belief it's

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:37.860
a business that turns on passion it's a business
that you just got to go with your instincts

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:41.589
and get your head out of the game sometimes
because this is the fear factor right this

00:07:41.589 --> 00:07:51.860
is the don't take risk factor speak the truth
and make friends with people if i can get

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:57.379
steven spielberg to want to buy a script i
mean he didn't gary goldstein's name i might

00:07:57.379 --> 00:08:03.569
as well have been the clerk at the local convenience
store right

00:08:03.569 --> 00:08:09.649
if an agent by the way had sent that very
